@0    = ~Ah... ssso you are the one who restored the Visionhive. I'm ssso glad to finally meet you, <CHARNAME>. I have heard of your prowessss, sssshaman.~
@1    = ~I welcome you to the grotto, emmisary. It's a pleasure to host you.~
@2    = ~Yeah, great. Why are you here, ghost?~
@3    = ~I can sssee that you know how to ssspeak with your guests, sssshaman.~
@4    = ~I can sssee you lack manners, <PRO_RACE>. A pity.~
@5    = ~I am here because we sssensed the Visionhive's energy was restored. And I sssse we were right. It has been ssso long sssince its fall. The followers of Amaunator knew how to ssseal its powers. But now -- now everything is going to change. Its energy hassss finally returned.~
@6    = ~We - the Eidolon Mists - would be pleased to negotiate a truce with you, sssshaman.~
@7    = ~A truce? Was there a war between your clan and the previous Visionhive shaman?~
@8    = ~I would like to know something more. What do you mean by "a truce"?~
@9    = ~Yesss - most unfortunately.~
@10   = ~Many yearssss ago, before the shadows, even before the Amaunatori, there was once a sssshaman who protected this place. Her name wasss Crytanner of the Brave. Sssshe began a bloody war with the intent of banishing usss, and wasss victorious. We left, but it's time to put an end this pointless conflict. It is time for usss to return.~
@11   = ~Why she wanted you gone? There must have been a reason.~
@12   = ~Hah! You really don't want to tell me why it actually happened, right?~
@13   = ~...~
@14   = ~We were accusssed of a traitorousss plan to take over this grotto. But that was falssse. We wanted to sssupport this place! We wanted it to be sssafe! But sssshe believed we sssought her death. That we wanted to sssee her fall. That was not--~
@15   = ~No. No more carelesssss words. Thissss conflict has already created too much hatred. We only wish to be under your protection, master sssshaman. Sssee our true intentionsss and let ussss join you in this magnificent place!~
@16   = ~(Focus on the grotto to ask it about its past and the Eidolon Mists clan.)~
@17   = ~I have a feeling that you're hiding something, dear emissary.~
@18   = ~Look at me. You should know how powerful I am. Tell me why are you really here.~
@19   = ~(When you focus upon the grotto, its roots and waters, you feel visions flowing to your mind, carried by invisible strings.~
@20   = ~(You can see a proud woman - Crytanner, the shaman who once served the Visionhive. She throws a clay mug filled with a black liquid, tainted with dark power. You see the emissary pointing a transparent finger at her; the spirits around them wail mournfully. They attempt to catch Crytanner, but she utters a chant which banishes them with a burst of blue-white energy.)~
@21   = ~(You focus - attempting to shape the images of the grotto, but your lack of experience means you are unable to piece them together into a cohesive story; perhaps if your mind were stronger, you would have succeeded. Your head is wracked with pain from the chaotic images.)~
@22   = ~You know that, do you? Ssso, did the grotto shown you visionsss, or did you guesss? This place should be ours. Let us in, and perhapsssss we may share its power. We deserve this place every bit assss much assss you!~
@23   = ~What--you wouldn't throw ussss away, would you? We only wisssh to live within. Allow usss to enter! We deserve this place every bit assss much assss you!~
@24   = ~I told you, shaman. We came here because we would like to ssset a truce. We have no bad intentions. Believe me.~
@25   = ~What else do you wisssh to know, shaman?~
@26   = ~I think you're hiding something, emissary.~
@27   = ~You haven't told me your name yet, emissary.~
@28   = ~Let's say I let your friends in and protect them just as I protect this grotto. What's in it for me?~
@29   = ~What was your relationship with Crytanner?~
@30   = ~I am ready to give you my answer.~
@31   = ~My apologies, shaman. I am known as Shy'glegh. But I do not see what my name has to do with this truce. I am but an emissary of my people.~
@32   = ~We are masters of wielding poisonous mists, shaman. We care little for honor, if poison may sssolve the problem more easily. Surely you could see the value of our assistance?~
@33   = ~Well, she wasn't fond of us or our powers, but times has changed... or am I wrong? The ssstrong must survive. The ssstrong shall rule.~
@34   = ~Ssso, do we have a deal, shaman? My people have waited too long.~
@35   = ~No, I don't trust you. I have a bad feeling about you and the Eidolon Mists.~
@36   = ~Yes. Summon your friends, emmisary. I permit you enter the grotto.~
@37   = ~What?! Cursed fool! You should have let ussss in! If you will not, then I will get rid of you on my own, weakling! Die!~
@38   = ~We thank you. We will come when the time is right. We shall meet sssoon.~
@39   = ~Hahahahahaha! Did you truly believe I would share this place with sssomeone like you? Foolish thing, you have opened this place for ussss, and now that you're no longer needed, it is time for you to die!~
@40   = ~I should have known it would eventually end like this. I will make you taste fear, ghost!~
@41   = ~I hoped you were better than this. Too bad I was wrong. Prepare to die.~
@42   = ~Wait, emmisary! It doesn't have to end like this!~
@43   = ~Hah, we shall sssee! Get <PRO_HIMHER>!~
@44   = ~Of course it does, fool. This place will be mine and mine alone! Die!~
